the target language is: prolog.

% Named variables: a variable phrase may carry a qualifier in front of its type
% so that several variables of the same type can be told apart. Here
% *a first person* and *a second person* are two DIFFERENT variables, both of
% type 'person' (the head noun). The all-caps id convention (e.g. *a person X*)
% still works too.

the templates are:
*a first person* greets *a second person*.
*a person* is sociable.

the ontology is:
    alice is a person.
    bob is a person.

the knowledge base demo includes:

a first person is sociable
    if the first person greets a second person
    and the first person is different from the second person.

scenario one is:
    alice greets bob.
    bob greets bob.
    one expects answers ["alice is sociable"].

query one is:
    which person is sociable.
